1
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:05,038
‪PREVIOUSLY ON <i>‪CHOSEN HOME</i>

2
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:07,741
<i>An animal lover</i>
<i>who's gentle-hearted and gay,</i>

3
00:00:07,807 --> 00:00:09,075
<i>Genichi Hatano,</i>

4
00:00:09,709 --> 00:00:12,645
<i>falls in love.</i>

5
00:00:12,712 --> 00:00:16,583
<i>His crush is a fellow gay man</i>
<i>and middle school teacher, Saku Sakuta.</i>

6
00:00:16,649 --> 00:00:18,351
I broke up with my partner
and ended our cohabitation.

7
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:20,520
<i>I was spending the night in my car.</i>

8
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:22,956
<i>Genichi wishes for Saku’s happiness.</i>

9
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,858
What do you think about buying a house?

10
00:00:24,924 --> 00:00:26,960
Maybe buying a house could be the "clamp".

11
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,428
Do as you like.

12
00:00:29,796 --> 00:00:32,732
<i>But Saku has a problematic student.</i>

13
00:00:32,799 --> 00:00:35,268
<i>Hotaru Kusunoki.</i>

14
00:00:35,335 --> 00:00:38,338
<i>She's a third-year middle schooler</i>
<i>who hangs around the red light district.</i>

15
00:00:41,274 --> 00:00:42,075
This is my dad.

16
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:44,544
Yes, he's my dad!

17
00:00:44,611 --> 00:00:45,445
I'm begging you.

18
00:00:45,512 --> 00:00:48,314
<i>For some reason, Hotaru wants him</i>
<i>to pretend to be her dad.</i>

19
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,850
<i>With the suitcase buried in the yard,</i>

20
00:00:50,917 --> 00:00:53,586
<i>Hotaru decides to pull off</i>
<i>the gamble of her lifetime.</i>

21
00:00:54,821 --> 00:00:56,923
- What the?
- Here is 30 million yen.

22
00:00:57,957 --> 00:00:59,993
You want a house, right?

23
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,729
I will… buy you.

24
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,933
- What do you mean, buy?
- With this money.

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,101
- Me, that is?
- Yes.

26
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:09,269
What do you mean?

27
00:01:09,335 --> 00:01:11,504
I'm saying I'll give you this money.

28
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,906
You then use it to buy a house,

29
00:01:12,972 --> 00:01:15,875
but in return, I want you
to pretend to be my dad.

30
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,911
- I don't get it.
- Like I said--

31
00:01:17,977 --> 00:01:20,113
First of all, what's this money?

32
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:21,981
- Whose is it?
- Ours.

33
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:26,719
Your mom. Where is she now?

34
00:01:27,687 --> 00:01:29,189
Can't you ask your dad from the other day?

35
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:32,292
I can tell you’ve got
your reasons in a way.

36
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:34,194
But you should talk to your teac--

37
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,129
I'm saying I don't want to!

38
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:37,197
Why not?

39
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:40,166
I’m not asking you
to become my real parent.

40
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:42,836
Just act the part when it’s needed.

41
00:01:42,902 --> 00:01:43,837
Come on now.

42
00:01:43,903 --> 00:01:45,472
Do you know what you're saying?

43
00:01:46,039 --> 00:01:47,373
It's not something I can just do.

44
00:01:48,675 --> 00:01:49,909
Why are you alone?

45
00:01:50,677 --> 00:01:52,846
At least tell me the reason.

46
00:01:52,912 --> 00:01:55,582
And this money.
Give me a proper explanation, okay?

47
00:01:56,082 --> 00:01:58,685
With this much, we could buy
a nice big house!

48
00:01:58,751 --> 00:01:59,853
One where the dogs could run around!

49
00:02:02,889 --> 00:02:04,190
Wouldn’t that be fun?

50
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:06,326
Hey, stop it. Let's put this away, yeah?

51
00:02:06,392 --> 00:02:08,328
And a big bath
where you can splash around!

52
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:12,632
- We don’t need that kind of house.
- Then what kind do you want?

53
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:17,570
I’m buying you,
so pick any house you like.

54
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,509
Coming! Please wait a moment.

55
00:02:22,575 --> 00:02:24,043
Hey, careful.

56
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:30,250
- Yes?
- Hello. Delivery service.

57
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:32,986
Please sign here.

58
00:02:33,052 --> 00:02:35,155
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

59
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:39,626
These are <i>shishamo</i> fish
from my parents in Hokkaido.

60
00:02:39,692 --> 00:02:42,162
They always send me tons
around this time of year.

61
00:02:42,228 --> 00:02:43,296
Oh yeah?

62
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:45,999
Want some? I'll share it with you.

63
00:02:46,065 --> 00:02:47,367
Thank you.

64
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,403
What do you usually eat?

65
00:02:51,137 --> 00:02:52,238
You live alone, right?

66
00:02:53,106 --> 00:02:56,075
- I just eat whatever.
- What about money? Your living expenses?

67
00:02:56,142 --> 00:02:58,378
- I'm fine.
- Really?

68
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:01,447
- Thank you for this.
- Huh?

69
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,751
- So, I’ll be counting on you.
- Wait, hey, your--

70
00:03:04,817 --> 00:03:07,420
- Thank you for having me.
- What?

71
00:03:13,459 --> 00:03:14,928
SHISHAMO WITH ROE

72
00:03:21,601 --> 00:03:25,071
There. We're good to go.

73
00:03:31,311 --> 00:03:32,445
Sorry, give me a second.

74
00:04:07,814 --> 00:04:08,681
What did I do with it?

75
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:10,984
Where is it?

76
00:04:11,784 --> 00:04:12,885
Looking for something?

77
00:04:15,555 --> 00:04:17,390
- No way!
- No way?

78
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:20,360
- Do you need some help?
- No, thank you.

79
00:04:23,796 --> 00:04:25,465
A sock, huh?

80
00:04:25,531 --> 00:04:29,302
They usually fall between the washer
and the wall, you know.

81
00:04:29,369 --> 00:04:33,172
Well, I don't have a house.
"Between the washer and the wall," sure.

82
00:04:35,541 --> 00:04:37,944
Um, about Yoshida…

83
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,147
Have you spoken to Hotaru
about her future?

84
00:04:41,814 --> 00:04:43,916
She'd better hand in
her career sheet soon.

85
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,029
I'll just wear this one.

86
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:04,203
Man, you're such a nuis--

87
00:05:07,407 --> 00:05:09,676
Someone was camping out in their car,
so I told them off.

88
00:05:09,742 --> 00:05:11,644
- Got it.
- I'll be on my way now.

89
00:05:11,711 --> 00:05:13,279
Thank you for your work.

90
00:05:16,382 --> 00:05:17,216
Something happened?

91
00:05:17,283 --> 00:05:20,920
Someone was camping out
in their car in the lot.

92
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:22,722
Security reported
that he gave them a warning.

93
00:05:22,789 --> 00:05:25,892
I hope they take it well though.

94
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:27,860
Right.

95
00:05:28,461 --> 00:05:30,830
LIST OF CAR CAMPING SPOTS IN TOKYO

96
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:32,598
I came to hand in the class journal.

97
00:05:35,101 --> 00:05:36,336
Thanks.

98
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,838
- Bye.
- Wait!

99
00:05:41,207 --> 00:05:43,309
Is he okay? I mean, your dad.

100
00:05:45,311 --> 00:05:46,346
What do you mean?

101
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,114
With stuff.

102
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:50,383
What stuff?

103
00:05:51,317 --> 00:05:52,151
Never mind.

104
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:54,620
If he's okay, then it's all good.

105
00:05:55,888 --> 00:05:59,258
Are you okay? Your socks don't match.

106
00:05:59,792 --> 00:06:00,626
Bye.

107
00:06:09,569 --> 00:06:11,304
TO KUSUNOKI. I’VE LIKED YOU

108
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:13,339
FOR A LONG TIME
PLEASE MEET ME BEHIND THE GYM

109
00:06:13,406 --> 00:06:14,374
AFTER SCHOOL ON MONDAY

110
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,680
How about homework?

111
00:06:29,689 --> 00:06:32,525
GAS BILL

112
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,972
TO KUSUNOKI
I’VE LIKED YOU FOR A LONG TIME…

113
00:06:57,617 --> 00:06:59,385
DAD

114
00:07:00,887 --> 00:07:02,455
INOKASHIRA APARTMENTS

115
00:07:02,522 --> 00:07:05,191
- Welcome back.
- I'm back.

116
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:07,727
How's the unit?
It's old, so I'm a little concerned.

117
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:09,162
- Are you fine with it?
- Yes.

118
00:07:09,796 --> 00:07:12,165
I’m content just having
a roof over my head.

119
00:07:16,569 --> 00:07:18,137
I'm back, Banana.

120
00:07:21,474 --> 00:07:23,242
Sorry, I need you to make way.

121
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:34,487
SAKUTA

122
00:07:41,427 --> 00:07:42,628
This is Hatano speaking.

123
00:07:42,695 --> 00:07:44,664
<i>This is Sakuta.</i>

124
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:47,967
- <i>Is everything okay?</i>
- What?

125
00:07:48,034 --> 00:07:50,303
The guard told you off
about sleeping in your car, right?

126
00:07:51,604 --> 00:07:53,539
More importantly, regarding Hotaru…

127
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,709
- <i>Are you listening?</i>
- Yes.

128
00:07:57,210 --> 00:07:58,144
<i>Three months ago,</i>

129
00:07:58,211 --> 00:07:59,745
<i>the police, Hotaru, and I</i>

130
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:01,214
<i>had a session.</i>

131
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,683
This time, we’d like her dad to join us.

132
00:08:04,417 --> 00:08:05,685
Wait, the police?

133
00:08:05,751 --> 00:08:08,488
The officer-in-charge is called Mr. Matsu.

134
00:08:09,088 --> 00:08:10,556
<i>You haven't met him before, right?</i>

135
00:08:11,357 --> 00:08:12,925
We’d like to go over the incident,

136
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:16,729
your current situation as her dad,
and other related matters.

137
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:19,098
When would be a good time for you?

138
00:08:20,366 --> 00:08:21,300
Well…

139
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,437
How about next Tuesday?

140
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,972
<i>Maybe around 6 p.m.?</i>

141
00:08:27,106 --> 00:08:28,574
- Okay.
- <i>See you then.</i>

142
00:08:29,442 --> 00:08:31,410
- Thank you.
- <i>See you.</i>

143
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:38,818
YOSHIDA: CAN WE MEET THIS WEEKEND?

144
00:08:43,956 --> 00:08:46,626
- Oh, Hotaru!
- Hey.

145
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:48,561
We're doing something fun!

146
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:50,062
Let me in on it.

147
00:08:50,730 --> 00:08:53,165
We’re doing a fake press conference!

148
00:08:54,734 --> 00:08:57,470
Which celebrity
does your fiancé look like?

149
00:08:57,537 --> 00:09:00,139
- He's just some old guy.
- Did you hear that?

150
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,641
What made you decide to get married?

151
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:03,876
- Huh? Marriage?!
- Well…

152
00:09:03,943 --> 00:09:07,380
- It's got to be his financial stability.
- Wait, are you getting married, Nacchi?

153
00:09:09,348 --> 00:09:11,217
Of course not!

154
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:13,586
Thank goodness.

155
00:09:13,653 --> 00:09:16,889
- You scared me!
- Did you believe it?

156
00:09:16,956 --> 00:09:19,058
- Tell us. Did you?
- Shut up!

157
00:09:19,125 --> 00:09:22,528
An older guy she got along well with
offered her a prenuptial agreement.

158
00:09:22,595 --> 00:09:23,596
Or so she said.

159
00:09:24,163 --> 00:09:25,398
What's that?

160
00:09:25,464 --> 00:09:27,800
I guess it's like a promise to marry
or something?

161
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:30,536
A "We’ll get married someday,
so let’s do our best" type of agreement.

162
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:32,004
- Cheers!
- Do your best!

163
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:32,939
Wait…

164
00:09:33,439 --> 00:09:36,442
If I sign the agreement,
he’ll give me 50,000 yen every month.

165
00:09:36,509 --> 00:09:39,312
I’ll take all the money I can,
and once it gets annoying,

166
00:09:39,378 --> 00:09:40,746
I'll just abandon him.

167
00:09:40,813 --> 00:09:42,615
- You're a genius!
- Genius idea!

168
00:09:42,682 --> 00:09:43,516
Hi-five!

169
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:44,584
Look at this!

170
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:48,688
"For indecent acts with a minor,

171
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,122
a man was arrested…"

172
00:09:50,189 --> 00:09:52,992
If it's proven the guy had
a prenuptial agreement with the girl

173
00:09:53,059 --> 00:09:55,394
and they were in
an engagement-like relationship,

174
00:09:55,461 --> 00:09:57,730
it may not be considered
a violation of law.

175
00:09:57,797 --> 00:10:00,166
- Meaning?
- Even if he does something gross to you,

176
00:10:00,232 --> 00:10:01,133
he might not get arrested!

177
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:03,703
- That's not good.
- Do you have the agreement with you?

178
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:04,937
No, it's with him.

179
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:07,473
What, you don't have it?

180
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,941
- No!
- What?

181
00:10:09,008 --> 00:10:10,876
CAREER SHEET

182
00:10:16,048 --> 00:10:17,850
Are you looking for Hotaru?

183
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:20,086
Yes.

184
00:10:20,152 --> 00:10:23,556
She usually doesn’t come back until
late at night on the days she goes out.

185
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:26,125
You'll probably have to wait
a little longer.

186
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:29,028
Um… Do you know her situation?

187
00:10:30,763 --> 00:10:31,831
‪Well,

188
00:10:31,897 --> 00:10:34,033
I mean, Hotaru's circumstances.

189
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:37,203
That's a secret.

190
00:10:37,269 --> 00:10:38,638
Right.

191
00:10:39,438 --> 00:10:40,306
NIKOMADO

192
00:10:40,373 --> 00:10:42,508
Speaking of which,
was everything okay the other day?

193
00:10:42,575 --> 00:10:44,577
I heard you had trouble with some kids.

194
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:48,547
Oh, that. They were collecting coins,

195
00:10:48,614 --> 00:10:50,449
so I thought they must be
really short on money.

196
00:10:50,516 --> 00:10:53,552
When I asked them,
"Is there anything you want?",

197
00:10:53,619 --> 00:10:55,254
they got creeped out.

198
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:57,790
Well, yeah.
It’s creepy and kinda annoying.

199
00:10:57,857 --> 00:10:59,291
Really?

200
00:11:00,226 --> 00:11:03,996
But I did clear the misunderstanding
with them later.

201
00:11:05,898 --> 00:11:07,433
There he is. Koinobori!

202
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,301
Oh, just as we speak of them.

203
00:11:11,303 --> 00:11:12,638
What's wrong?

204
00:11:12,705 --> 00:11:15,641
- Hey, won't you marry me too?
- Me too, please!

205
00:11:15,708 --> 00:11:16,909
- You too?
- No, me.

206
00:11:16,976 --> 00:11:18,577
- So hard to decide…
- Please!

207
00:11:18,644 --> 00:11:20,546
- Please!
- Pretty please!

208
00:11:20,613 --> 00:11:23,115
- How old are you, anyway?
- Well, I'm…

209
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,550
Sorry for interrupting.

210
00:11:25,384 --> 00:11:28,387
Hello. I’m with Nikomado,
from the Niko Consultation Desk.

211
00:11:28,454 --> 00:11:31,957
I heard about what happened.
So, what’s this prenuptial agreement?

212
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:34,193
Let’s go to the police together.

213
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:36,929
I don't wanna!

214
00:11:36,996 --> 00:11:38,497
Hand it over!

215
00:11:38,998 --> 00:11:41,100
Nicely done!

216
00:11:41,167 --> 00:11:42,068
This?

217
00:11:42,134 --> 00:11:43,369
That's not it.

218
00:11:43,436 --> 00:11:44,470
- This!
- Yes!

219
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,172
Let's get out of here!

220
00:11:46,238 --> 00:11:47,673
Quick!

221
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:48,941
Wait!

222
00:11:49,008 --> 00:11:50,209
- Where are you going?
- Hey!

223
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,048
PARKING
2,000 YEN FOR THE FIRST 24 HOURS

224
00:11:56,115 --> 00:11:57,683
That's so expensive!

225
00:12:04,590 --> 00:12:05,558
Time to sleep.

226
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:27,113
So, I suggested we buy a house

227
00:12:27,179 --> 00:12:30,015
and make it our "family glue".

228
00:12:30,816 --> 00:12:32,318
Guess what? He said I'm scaring him.

229
00:12:32,384 --> 00:12:33,986
He's got a point.

230
00:12:34,053 --> 00:12:36,856
But the one who said "love and revolution"
and "family glue"

231
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:40,426
was you, Ms. Momose.
That really lit a fire in me!

232
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:41,694
Oh, no.

233
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:45,097
I assumed it was for the sake
of your partner.

234
00:12:45,698 --> 00:12:48,334
I don’t have anyone like that.

235
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:51,370
Then, can I take it that you're here today
to join the membership?

236
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:52,671
Hang on…

237
00:12:53,172 --> 00:12:55,641
Looking back,

238
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:59,044
I think I suggested the "family glue" idea
because I wanted that person to be happy.

239
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:02,181
So, I can’t actually join.

240
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:05,484
Does that mean it’s already started?

241
00:13:05,551 --> 00:13:08,621
It might have already started… I think.

242
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:11,023
- Lots of things.
- Really?

243
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:13,125
You know…

244
00:13:14,093 --> 00:13:15,594
- A kid…
- Wait, did you say, kid?

245
00:13:16,162 --> 00:13:17,663
Your partner has a child?

246
00:13:17,730 --> 00:13:19,431
It's not exactly that.

247
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:24,103
- I don’t quite understand the situation.
- Me neither.

248
00:13:26,238 --> 00:13:29,375
I love parfaits.

249
00:13:30,209 --> 00:13:31,110
Why all of a sudden?

250
00:13:32,178 --> 00:13:34,947
To me, a parfait is life.

251
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:37,850
The cream, the fruits, the cereal.

252
00:13:37,917 --> 00:13:40,853
They all stack together
to make the parfait, right?

253
00:13:41,587 --> 00:13:44,089
Similarly, life is made up

254
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:46,325
of the accumulation of what we do
in the present.

255
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,495
If you do what you can

256
00:13:49,562 --> 00:13:52,698
and what you should now,

257
00:13:52,765 --> 00:13:55,835
eventually, you’ll realize
you’ve made a proper parfait.

258
00:13:56,869 --> 00:13:58,003
Is that…

259
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:00,706
from Dazai or something too?

260
00:14:00,773 --> 00:14:04,009
No. It's Momose's original quote.

261
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:05,978
Where is it?

262
00:14:06,779 --> 00:14:09,081
- Looking for something?
- Yeah.

263
00:14:09,148 --> 00:14:12,852
Have you seen a Santa-patterned sock?

264
00:14:12,918 --> 00:14:15,387
- Nope.
- Maybe over there.

265
00:14:16,622 --> 00:14:19,558
- Is it that important?
- I don't know.

266
00:14:19,625 --> 00:14:21,293
I'm just searching for it for no reason.

267
00:14:22,394 --> 00:14:23,429
Why?

268
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:25,397
For my parfait.

269
00:14:33,339 --> 00:14:36,308
Welcome home. I mean, please come on in.

270
00:14:37,476 --> 00:14:39,678
- Thank you for having me.
- Wear these.

271
00:14:45,117 --> 00:14:46,585
Did you rearrange the place?

272
00:14:46,652 --> 00:14:49,855
Well, duh. Also, those are your things.

273
00:14:49,922 --> 00:14:52,925
The stuff in the bathroom…
I couldn’t tell whose was whose,

274
00:14:52,992 --> 00:14:54,093
so just take yours back.

275
00:14:54,159 --> 00:14:56,695
You're the type to delete all photos
after breaking up.

276
00:14:56,762 --> 00:14:58,864
I throw away all the gifts too.

277
00:15:00,132 --> 00:15:02,368
- I thought this was about Hatano.
- What?

278
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,137
Didn't he come
with the marriage registration?

279
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,506
Oh yeah, he did.

280
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,541
But seriously, don't go passing that
to randoms.

281
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,911
I didn't think he'd go see you.

282
00:15:12,778 --> 00:15:16,448
In the end, I still don’t know
why he came.

283
00:15:16,515 --> 00:15:17,583
What did you talk about?

284
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:21,453
Can’t remember much… What was it again?

285
00:15:22,788 --> 00:15:24,890
He said he wanted to fall madly in love.

286
00:15:26,225 --> 00:15:29,528
- He told me to buy a house.
- Huh?

287
00:15:30,663 --> 00:15:32,531
He said you and I
should buy a house together,

288
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:35,801
and use that as a clamp,
so we’d always be together.

289
00:15:35,868 --> 00:15:36,835
How does that work?

290
00:15:36,902 --> 00:15:40,272
- I don’t know.
- He's crazy.

291
00:15:40,339 --> 00:15:41,907
I know, right?

292
00:15:46,345 --> 00:15:47,513
Are you done?

293
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:52,318
This is everything.

294
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:57,790
Why don't we stay together
until we can file the marriage papers?

295
00:15:59,992 --> 00:16:02,394
What? You're being a creep.

296
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,531
- Figured.
- See you.

297
00:16:06,098 --> 00:16:06,999
Thanks for having me.

298
00:16:08,567 --> 00:16:09,468
See you.

299
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:17,676
Hey! Wait here.

300
00:16:21,947 --> 00:16:23,082
Are you okay?

301
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:26,919
Dang it!

302
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:29,054
- Open the door!
- No, I'm fine!

303
00:16:29,121 --> 00:16:30,723
- Just open the goddamn door!
- Ugh!

304
00:16:34,593 --> 00:16:35,494
If you don't mind me…

305
00:16:38,697 --> 00:16:39,999
Get out of the way!

306
00:16:41,266 --> 00:16:43,936
It's a good thing the fire didn’t spread.

307
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,637
You could say that again.

308
00:16:45,704 --> 00:16:48,173
I was grilling the <i>shishamo</i> fish,
and it exploded into flames.

309
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:51,543
<i>Shishamo?</i>
You've got quite the refined taste.

310
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:53,012
I shared some with her.

311
00:16:53,612 --> 00:16:54,847
It came from Hokkaido.

312
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,849
Is that so?

313
00:16:57,750 --> 00:17:00,119
Sorry, I didn’t teach her
how to cook them properly.

314
00:17:00,753 --> 00:17:02,254
I'm sorry for the trouble.

315
00:17:02,321 --> 00:17:03,822
It’s totally fine,

316
00:17:04,656 --> 00:17:06,625
but I don’t get any <i>shishamo,</i> huh?

317
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,227
Huh?

318
00:17:09,595 --> 00:17:12,464
I see how it is.
<i>Shishamo</i> from Hokkaido, huh?

319
00:17:13,332 --> 00:17:16,635
That's cool. It must be good <i>shishamo.</i>

320
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:19,438
- Maybe it's <i>karafuto shishamo.</i>
- I'll bring some to her.

321
00:17:19,505 --> 00:17:20,672
- You'd better.
- Right.

322
00:17:25,444 --> 00:17:26,678
Let's clean this up, yeah?

323
00:17:26,745 --> 00:17:29,048
- I can do it by myself.
- Don't be shy.

324
00:17:33,485 --> 00:17:37,389
Genichi, the guy living below,
how are things with him?

325
00:17:38,590 --> 00:17:41,093
Sometimes I hear him playing the guitar.

326
00:17:42,995 --> 00:17:43,862
Think it's noisy?

327
00:17:45,431 --> 00:17:46,598
Not really.

328
00:17:47,766 --> 00:17:50,135
Aren't his songs amazing?

329
00:17:50,869 --> 00:17:52,237
I don't know.

330
00:17:52,304 --> 00:17:54,706
He was once offered the chance to debut.

331
00:17:55,374 --> 00:17:56,308
Really?

332
00:17:57,142 --> 00:17:58,343
As a musician, that is.

333
00:17:59,278 --> 00:18:00,479
I'm proud of him as a friend.

334
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:10,022
Take care. Say hi to your parents for me.

335
00:18:11,056 --> 00:18:11,890
Okay.

336
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:15,127
- Thanks. See you.
- See you.

337
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,401
Wanna try grilling the <i>shishamo</i> again?

338
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:29,208
If you make a hole like this
before grilling,

339
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:30,676
they won’t explode.

340
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:36,615
- Like this?
- Yes.

341
00:18:39,284 --> 00:18:41,120
I got a call from Sakuta.

342
00:18:41,753 --> 00:18:44,590
- About the other day?
- It's about another matter.

343
00:18:44,656 --> 00:18:46,959
The one with Mr. Matsu from the police.

344
00:18:47,025 --> 00:18:51,230
Apparently there’s a meeting with him,
you, me, and your teacher.

345
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:53,866
Why are the police involved?

346
00:18:53,932 --> 00:18:56,101
Is it about your mom or dad?

347
00:18:56,168 --> 00:18:57,569
Something like that.

348
00:18:59,771 --> 00:19:02,141
It's going to be next Tuesday,
6 p.m., at school.

349
00:19:02,207 --> 00:19:04,610
We’ll tell them the truth

350
00:19:05,177 --> 00:19:07,045
- and get some advice from your teacher.
- No!

351
00:19:07,779 --> 00:19:09,148
I absolutely don't wanna.

352
00:19:10,449 --> 00:19:11,517
I won't go then.

353
00:19:12,017 --> 00:19:15,254
Look, could you tell me what happened?

354
00:19:15,954 --> 00:19:18,891
About the incident, the police, the money…

355
00:19:18,957 --> 00:19:22,261
I don’t know anything.
So, please, give me the rundown.

356
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:25,731
Okay!

357
00:19:25,797 --> 00:19:28,800
I’ll tell you everything,
only if you'll pretend to be my parent.

358
00:19:28,867 --> 00:19:30,636
- Now that's--
- Please!

359
00:19:32,704 --> 00:19:36,008
Or you can just listen
and think about it for now.

360
00:19:36,074 --> 00:19:38,343
- Well yeah, I'll think about it, but…
- You will?

361
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:39,845
That's not what I meant.

362
00:19:39,912 --> 00:19:42,114
- I'll go and get ready.
- Get ready?

363
00:19:44,783 --> 00:19:46,985
Oh, and before I forget. This.

364
00:19:47,052 --> 00:19:48,420
CAREER SHEET

365
00:19:48,487 --> 00:19:49,888
He said to submit it.

366
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:52,624
Ever filled one out before?

367
00:19:53,258 --> 00:19:54,426
Well, yeah.

368
00:19:54,493 --> 00:19:56,528
What did you write
when you were in middle school?

369
00:19:58,430 --> 00:19:59,531
Musician.

370
00:20:00,832 --> 00:20:01,867
Makes sense.

371
00:20:02,734 --> 00:20:04,603
You like music.

372
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:06,538
You don’t have anything you like?

373
00:20:07,406 --> 00:20:08,373
I don't know.

374
00:20:09,641 --> 00:20:10,876
I see.

375
00:20:11,910 --> 00:20:12,878
Okay, let’s eat.

376
00:20:14,413 --> 00:20:16,081
- Thanks for the meal.
- Not at all.

377
00:20:26,692 --> 00:20:27,526
It's tasty.

378
00:20:28,927 --> 00:20:30,162
I'm glad to hear that.

379
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:35,500
<i>Fifty-five minutes</i>
<i>to Zenpukuji Middle School.</i>

380
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,935
So, I need to wake up at 5 a.m.?

381
00:20:39,471 --> 00:20:41,974
<i>Today’s place to sleep</i>

382
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:45,244
<i>Is on a park bench</i>

383
00:20:45,310 --> 00:20:47,779
<i>Sleeping in cramped spots</i>

384
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:51,483
<i>Is what you're used to</i>

385
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:57,122
<i>Tomorrow’s place will be in a car</i>

386
00:20:57,189 --> 00:20:58,757
<i>Fallen</i>

387
00:20:58,824 --> 00:21:05,530
<i>Leaves will wrap you up</i>

388
00:21:09,001 --> 00:21:09,835
Hang in there, me.

389
00:21:09,901 --> 00:21:12,271
<i>No home</i>

390
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:15,474
<i>Oh, no home</i>

391
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:18,377
<i>The vast sky</i>

392
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:20,579
<i>Is your roof</i>

393
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:24,049
<i>The day after tomorrow…</i>

394
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:26,184
<i>The day after tomorrow…</i>

395
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:32,257
<i>Let's go look for your new home</i>

396
00:21:32,758 --> 00:21:34,059
- Bye.
- Bye.

397
00:21:36,728 --> 00:21:37,796
Bye.

398
00:21:38,997 --> 00:21:41,667
Will you have your career sheet
ready by Tuesday?

399
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:45,604
- Yes.
- This time, no blanks, okay?

400
00:21:45,671 --> 00:21:46,505
Okay.

401
00:21:47,406 --> 00:21:50,475
Are you getting along well with your dad?

402
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:53,979
He grilled <i>shishamo</i> for me.

403
00:21:54,046 --> 00:21:56,181
He also taught me
how to prevent them from exploding.

404
00:21:57,382 --> 00:21:59,518
- They explode?
- With a bang.

405
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,920
Please be careful too.

406
00:22:02,954 --> 00:22:05,090
<i>Shishamo…</i> explode?

407
00:22:08,527 --> 00:22:11,330
PRENUPTIAL AGREEMENT

408
00:22:11,396 --> 00:22:12,230
Uh…

409
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:15,167
Who's this "party A"?

410
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:17,769
It refers to that guy.

411
00:22:17,836 --> 00:22:19,638
And "party B" is you.

412
00:22:20,305 --> 00:22:23,241
Then, why can't he write "me" and "you"?

413
00:22:23,308 --> 00:22:25,344
- You're right.
- Kinda stupid, huh?

414
00:22:25,410 --> 00:22:28,113
Adults are so lame!

415
00:22:30,949 --> 00:22:32,651
31,500,000 YEN

416
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:34,419
Coming.

417
00:22:35,921 --> 00:22:37,089
I'm ready.

418
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:41,126
Okay, let’s read through this together.

419
00:22:41,827 --> 00:22:42,761
Parent-Child Contract.

420
00:22:42,828 --> 00:22:43,795
PARENT-CHILD CONTRACT

421
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:49,735
From this point forward, Hotaru Kusunoki,

422
00:22:49,801 --> 00:22:51,069
hereafter referred to as "Party A",

423
00:22:51,136 --> 00:22:53,505
and Genichi Hatano,
hereafter referred to as "Party B",

424
00:22:53,572 --> 00:22:55,240
agree to enter

425
00:22:55,307 --> 00:22:58,243
into the following terms
of a parent-child contract,

426
00:22:58,310 --> 00:23:00,779
hereafter referred to as "this Contract".

427
00:23:00,846 --> 00:23:03,181
Now, hold on. What is this?

428
00:23:03,248 --> 00:23:04,549
It's a contract.

429
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:06,284
You've got to be joking…

430
00:23:07,085 --> 00:23:08,353
You can sign at the end.

431
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:11,490
- Article One…
- Wait!

432
00:23:12,257 --> 00:23:13,458
You’d think about it, right?

433
00:23:13,525 --> 00:23:15,260
Well, yeah. But…

434
00:23:15,327 --> 00:23:18,096
I’ll tell you everything,
so please listen till the end.

435
00:23:18,163 --> 00:23:19,431
Okay.

436
00:23:19,931 --> 00:23:22,367
Article One. Purpose.

437
00:23:23,001 --> 00:23:26,004
Under all circumstances, Party A
and Party B shall support one another

438
00:23:26,638 --> 00:23:30,275
and strive to maintain a harmonious
pretend parent-child relationship.

439
00:23:30,342 --> 00:23:32,477
The parties enter
into this agreement for this purpose.

440
00:23:33,011 --> 00:23:35,046
Article Two. Agreement.

441
00:23:35,547 --> 00:23:37,816
Party A and Party B
hereby agree on October 20th,

442
00:23:37,883 --> 00:23:41,286
2025, to enter
into a parent-child contract.

443
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:44,689
Article Three. About Party A. First,

444
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:46,858
Party A was born on August 26,

445
00:23:46,925 --> 00:23:49,861
2010, 15 years old.

446
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:52,798
Third-year student
at Zenpukuji Middle School, Class 4.

447
00:23:53,298 --> 00:23:55,801
Second, they currently reside
at Inokashira Apartments,

448
00:23:55,867 --> 00:23:57,803
Room 206.

449
00:23:58,537 --> 00:24:01,106
Three, their father, Jin Ichigaya,

450
00:24:01,173 --> 00:24:04,209
divorced when Party A was nine
and has since left home.

451
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:07,646
He remarried and started a new family,
so he’s not someone they can rely on.

452
00:24:08,647 --> 00:24:10,515
That was the man from the crepe place?

453
00:24:10,582 --> 00:24:13,485
I actually wanted him to come
to my parent-teacher conference,

454
00:24:13,552 --> 00:24:16,021
but it was apparently
inconvenient for him.

455
00:24:16,087 --> 00:24:17,889
I don’t matter to him anymore.

456
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:21,726
- Anyway, moving on.
- Uh, okay.

457
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,196
Four, Party A’s mother, Tomoe Kusunoki,

458
00:24:24,262 --> 00:24:27,833
is currently wanted for embezzlement
from her company and is on the run.

459
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:32,070
She stole money and is on the run.

460
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,105
Since then, I’ve been on my own.

461
00:24:34,706 --> 00:24:36,141
MOM

462
00:24:40,512 --> 00:24:42,948
- Hello?
- <i>Morning, Hotaru.</i>

463
00:24:43,014 --> 00:24:44,516
Mom?

464
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:47,118
<i>Listen, I won’t be coming home</i>
<i>for a while.</i>

465
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:49,654
<i>I’m sorry.</i>

466
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,290
<i>There’s a bankbook on the desk.</i>

467
00:24:52,357 --> 00:24:54,759
<i>For the time being,</i>
<i>use that money carefully, okay?</i>

468
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:56,962
<i>With the landlady,</i>

469
00:24:57,596 --> 00:24:59,764
<i>I left a suitcase.</i>

470
00:25:00,799 --> 00:25:03,969
<i>What’s inside belongs to us.</i>

471
00:25:04,736 --> 00:25:06,271
Us?

472
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:08,373
<i>Until I'm back,</i>

473
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:11,376
<i>I’m leaving it in your care. I'll be back.</i>

474
00:25:12,911 --> 00:25:13,845
Okay.

475
00:25:14,846 --> 00:25:17,082
But not long after that, the police came.

476
00:25:17,148 --> 00:25:20,051
They said my mom stole money and ran off

477
00:25:20,118 --> 00:25:21,653
and asked if I knew where she was.

478
00:25:22,153 --> 00:25:23,788
Like I'd believe that, right?

479
00:25:25,490 --> 00:25:29,027
But they kept asking and asking,
and it started to sound like it was true.

480
00:25:30,629 --> 00:25:32,063
<i>The police searched the apartment,</i>

481
00:25:32,130 --> 00:25:33,265
<i>looking for the money.</i>

482
00:25:33,932 --> 00:25:36,668
<i>It used to be just me and Mom</i>
<i>living there,</i>

483
00:25:36,735 --> 00:25:39,371
<i>but little by little, it started to feel</i>
<i>like someone else’s home.</i>

484
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:42,974
<i>Soon after, someone</i>
<i>from the child guidance center came.</i>

485
00:25:43,475 --> 00:25:45,877
Regarding your situation going forward…

486
00:25:47,012 --> 00:25:49,314
Since you can’t live alone,

487
00:25:49,814 --> 00:25:52,250
if your dad or relatives

488
00:25:53,151 --> 00:25:55,754
can't take you in,

489
00:25:56,254 --> 00:25:58,256
we’ll need to find a facility for you.

490
00:25:58,323 --> 00:25:59,291
I'm good.

491
00:25:59,357 --> 00:26:02,527
My mom said on the phone
that she’d only be gone for a while.

492
00:26:02,594 --> 00:26:03,495
So,

493
00:26:03,995 --> 00:26:05,897
she’ll come back eventually.

494
00:26:05,964 --> 00:26:08,066
I’ll stay here and wait.

495
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:10,035
I understand how you feel,

496
00:26:10,101 --> 00:26:12,470
but for now, let’s head
to the facility, okay?

497
00:26:13,605 --> 00:26:14,739
Ms. Kusunoki?

498
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:18,043
My dad.

499
00:26:18,109 --> 00:26:20,278
My dad who left after the divorce.

500
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:23,315
He saw the news and called.

501
00:26:24,849 --> 00:26:27,085
He said he’s coming back.

502
00:26:27,719 --> 00:26:28,553
So,

503
00:26:29,321 --> 00:26:30,555
I do have a guardian.

504
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:32,424
I'll be fine.

505
00:26:33,224 --> 00:26:34,159
<i>I lied.</i>

506
00:26:34,225 --> 00:26:36,861
Surprisingly, she believed me.

507
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:39,397
I didn’t have to go to the facility.

508
00:26:40,699 --> 00:26:43,969
After that, I received the suitcase
from the landlady.

509
00:26:44,035 --> 00:26:46,905
<i>It seems she had just been</i>
<i>holding on to it for me.</i>

510
00:26:48,373 --> 00:26:50,342
<i>Then, when I opened it…</i>

511
00:27:01,586 --> 00:27:02,420
One…

512
00:27:04,089 --> 00:27:04,923
two…

513
00:27:06,858 --> 00:27:08,026
three…

514
00:27:16,935 --> 00:27:20,038
32 million 261 thousand and 570 yen…

515
00:27:20,105 --> 00:27:21,940
ESTIMATED EMBEZZLED FUNDS 32,261,570 YEN

516
00:27:22,540 --> 00:27:26,311
For the time being, I buried the suitcase
in the yard, so no one would find it.

517
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:28,880
For quite some time, the police

518
00:27:28,947 --> 00:27:31,549
and the child guidance people
would drop by to check on me,

519
00:27:32,183 --> 00:27:34,119
but I just pretended not to be home.

520
00:27:36,021 --> 00:27:38,523
<i>Since my phone is cut off,</i>

521
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:40,725
<i>this is the only place anyone</i>
<i>could find me.</i>

522
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:43,161
Not that anyone does.

523
00:27:44,829 --> 00:27:47,832
So, I kept living by myself,
making sure nobody knows about it.

524
00:27:47,899 --> 00:27:49,701
I even lied to my school

525
00:27:49,768 --> 00:27:52,203
- and went about my classes as usual, but…
- Here.

526
00:27:52,771 --> 00:27:53,872
We wrote this for you.

527
00:27:53,938 --> 00:27:55,206
WE’RE STILL FRIENDS!
EVERYONE LIKES YOU!

528
00:27:56,274 --> 00:27:57,108
- I don't want it.
- Why?

529
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:59,310
Just act like you usually do around me.

530
00:27:59,377 --> 00:28:01,513
- But we saw the news--
- I don't need it!

531
00:28:01,579 --> 00:28:03,748
- It's our heartfelt--
- I said I don't need it!

532
00:28:05,316 --> 00:28:07,719
Isn't that mean?

533
00:28:10,955 --> 00:28:13,692
Everyone kept looking at me with pity,
and I really hated it.

534
00:28:14,826 --> 00:28:16,561
I feel at ease in Toyoko.

535
00:28:17,629 --> 00:28:18,897
<i>I can talk about anything there.</i>

536
00:28:19,831 --> 00:28:22,000
<i>No one treats me like I’m different.</i>

537
00:28:22,667 --> 00:28:26,271
When I told them that my mom
embezzled money, they just laughed it off.

538
00:28:26,771 --> 00:28:28,173
They found it amusing and wild.

539
00:28:28,940 --> 00:28:31,609
They didn’t put up walls
like the kids at school did.

540
00:28:31,676 --> 00:28:33,845
I felt comfortable there. But…

541
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:38,249
with things like student-parent meetings,
and the meeting tomorrow,

542
00:28:38,316 --> 00:28:40,418
it’s getting harder without a dad lately.

543
00:28:41,119 --> 00:28:41,953
That’s why…

544
00:28:42,687 --> 00:28:44,622
I need someone to pretend to be my parent.

545
00:28:48,093 --> 00:28:49,828
That's the gist of my situation.

546
00:28:51,596 --> 00:28:53,965
Article Four. Payment.

547
00:28:54,799 --> 00:28:57,635
As compensation, Party A shall pay Party B

548
00:28:57,702 --> 00:28:59,738
32,261,570 yen

549
00:28:59,804 --> 00:29:01,940
for entering this contract.

550
00:29:03,308 --> 00:29:05,443
Article Five. Confidentiality.

551
00:29:05,510 --> 00:29:07,045
Both parties shall keep

552
00:29:07,112 --> 00:29:10,014
this contract strictly confidential

553
00:29:10,081 --> 00:29:13,418
and may not disclose it to any third party
without prior consent.

554
00:29:13,952 --> 00:29:16,221
Article Six. Promises.

555
00:29:16,888 --> 00:29:20,158
Both Party A and Party B
agree not to lie to each other.

556
00:29:21,126 --> 00:29:22,193
That’s all.

557
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:25,563
PARTY A, PARTY B

558
00:29:25,630 --> 00:29:27,298
Please sign here.

559
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:31,669
In any case, I just want to wait
for my mom here.

560
00:29:31,736 --> 00:29:34,639
I know she didn’t do it.
There must be a reason.

561
00:29:35,306 --> 00:29:37,175
It's just half a year more
until I graduate.

562
00:29:37,675 --> 00:29:41,646
I’ll take care of my own living.
I just need you to act the part sometimes.

563
00:29:42,814 --> 00:29:43,882
So, please.

564
00:29:49,254 --> 00:29:50,321
Hey…

565
00:29:50,922 --> 00:29:53,758
Even if you do manage
to graduate, what then?

566
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:54,826
I don't know.

567
00:29:54,893 --> 00:29:56,961
You can’t keep living alone here.

568
00:29:57,028 --> 00:29:57,929
I can!

569
00:29:59,531 --> 00:30:01,099
Playing pretend won’t last long.

570
00:30:01,166 --> 00:30:02,300
I'll make sure it does!

571
00:30:02,367 --> 00:30:06,638
You can wait for your mom, sure.
But there has to be another way.

572
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:08,873
Is there?

573
00:30:13,778 --> 00:30:16,548
In any case, tomorrow,
let’s tell your teacher and the police

574
00:30:17,148 --> 00:30:19,684
- the truth, okay?
- Forget it. We're done here.

575
00:30:20,885 --> 00:30:21,719
Hey, wait!

576
00:30:37,235 --> 00:30:39,904
I’VE LIKED YOU FOR A LONG TIME
MEET ME BEHIND THE GYM ON MONDAY

577
00:30:41,940 --> 00:30:43,141
ELECTRICITY: 3,762 YEN; GAS: 1,486 YEN

578
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:44,442
WATER: 1,774 YEN
PHONE BILL, FOOD AND TRAIN FARE…

579
00:30:49,547 --> 00:30:50,982
- A minute ago…
- You were sleeping.

580
00:30:51,883 --> 00:30:53,051
Kusunoki.

581
00:30:54,018 --> 00:30:56,554
After class, come to the reception room
on the second floor.

582
00:30:57,655 --> 00:30:58,656
Okay.

583
00:31:01,226 --> 00:31:03,595
Did your dad say he'll be late?

584
00:31:09,334 --> 00:31:10,568
Sorry for being late.

585
00:31:11,069 --> 00:31:12,904
I couldn't quite find my way here.

586
00:31:13,404 --> 00:31:16,140
We've been expecting you.
This is police officer…

587
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:17,675
I'm Matsu. Nice to meet you.

588
00:31:20,044 --> 00:31:21,012
Thank you

589
00:31:21,579 --> 00:31:23,715
- for taking care of my daughter.
- Huh?

590
00:31:27,285 --> 00:31:28,286
Please have a seat.

591
00:31:30,021 --> 00:31:31,022
Thank you.

592
00:31:36,327 --> 00:31:39,564
Today, we’d like to go over
Hotaru’s future living arrangements

593
00:31:39,631 --> 00:31:42,300
and have you, her dad,
to review and confirm them.

594
00:31:42,367 --> 00:31:43,801
- Okay.
- Together with the school

595
00:31:43,868 --> 00:31:47,171
and the child guidance center,
we, as the police, want to coordinate

596
00:31:47,238 --> 00:31:49,540
and support her life going forward.

597
00:31:50,108 --> 00:31:51,309
Right.

598
00:31:51,376 --> 00:31:54,245
Please support Ms. Hotaru
until she's at the age to live on her own.

599
00:31:54,879 --> 00:31:56,381
- I understand.
- Okay.

600
00:31:56,447 --> 00:32:00,084
To start things off, could you please
tell us your name once again?

601
00:32:00,652 --> 00:32:02,186
Genichi Hatano.

602
00:32:02,887 --> 00:32:03,721
Oops…

603
00:32:04,222 --> 00:32:05,056
Hatano?

604
00:32:06,491 --> 00:32:10,328
That’s different from the name Ms. Hotaru
mentioned in the previous meeting.

605
00:32:12,096 --> 00:32:13,097
What's going on?

606
00:32:15,366 --> 00:32:16,401
Uh…

607
00:32:18,403 --> 00:32:21,639
That’s my name after remarriage.

608
00:32:21,706 --> 00:32:23,207
Your first name is different too.

609
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:26,177
Didn’t you say, "Genichi"?

610
00:32:29,213 --> 00:32:32,951
I m-misspoke. That’s… Well, um…

611
00:32:34,886 --> 00:32:35,787
my stage name.

612
00:32:35,853 --> 00:32:37,588
- Stage name?
- What?

613
00:32:38,489 --> 00:32:42,694
Yes. I used to aim to be a musician.

614
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:46,164
I didn't manage to debut, but I was close.

615
00:32:46,230 --> 00:32:49,500
Sometimes I still use that name.

616
00:32:49,567 --> 00:32:51,502
It kinda stuck with me.

617
00:32:53,404 --> 00:32:55,106
Besides, in name fortune-telling,

618
00:32:55,173 --> 00:32:58,009
"Genichi Hatano" supposedly brings
better luck, so…

619
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:02,547
- Wait, so your real name is different?
- Oh,

620
00:33:02,613 --> 00:33:03,548
my real name?

621
00:33:03,614 --> 00:33:04,582
It's…

622
00:33:09,587 --> 00:33:12,023
Jin Ichigaya.

623
00:33:14,359 --> 00:33:15,660
Mr. Jin Ichigaya…

624
00:33:17,395 --> 00:33:18,963
Your stage name is Genichi Hatano?

625
00:33:24,235 --> 00:33:25,336
True, it has a ring to it.

626
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:30,475
But Jin Ichigaya

627
00:33:30,541 --> 00:33:32,510
also sounds like
a talented actor's name, right?

628
00:33:32,577 --> 00:33:34,579
- Well, yeah…
- Right?

629
00:33:35,980 --> 00:33:37,415
You're hurting Dad's feelings.

630
00:33:38,116 --> 00:33:39,250
I'm sorry.

631
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:43,588
And what's the status between you
and her mom, Tomoe Kusunoki?

632
00:33:44,655 --> 00:33:46,891
When she was nine,

633
00:33:46,958 --> 00:33:49,560
we divorced, and I haven’t seen her since.

634
00:33:50,061 --> 00:33:52,030
And both of you are now living together.

635
00:33:53,331 --> 00:33:54,632
Yes, that's right.

636
00:33:55,566 --> 00:33:57,969
As to why you hadn’t been in touch
all this time,

637
00:33:58,036 --> 00:33:59,637
was there perhaps some reason?

638
00:34:00,505 --> 00:34:02,740
I just wasn't aware of anything,

639
00:34:02,807 --> 00:34:05,376
whether about the case

640
00:34:05,443 --> 00:34:06,744
or about what was going on.

641
00:34:07,412 --> 00:34:09,647
But she told me everything.

642
00:34:11,582 --> 00:34:14,419
Even the painful things,
she shared it all…

643
00:34:14,485 --> 00:34:17,121
So, I want her

644
00:34:17,822 --> 00:34:20,291
to focus not on daily stuff, meals,

645
00:34:20,925 --> 00:34:22,994
or even money,

646
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:27,331
but on what she likes, who she likes…

647
00:34:27,398 --> 00:34:31,035
I want her to be preoccupied
with things like that as much as possible.

648
00:34:31,669 --> 00:34:32,670
That’s why

649
00:34:34,172 --> 00:34:35,206
I decided

650
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:38,309
to be a father to her.

651
00:34:39,243 --> 00:34:42,346
One more time, I mean.

652
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:43,915
Very well.

653
00:34:45,116 --> 00:34:46,951
So, her daily life seems fine.

654
00:34:48,719 --> 00:34:52,156
Next, a few questions about the case.

655
00:34:54,926 --> 00:34:56,294
I'll go get my bag from class.

656
00:35:00,231 --> 00:35:01,732
I'll be taking my leave now.

657
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:04,702
- I’ll see you to the exit.
- Thank you. It's fine.

658
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:05,837
Well then.

659
00:35:09,807 --> 00:35:11,642
I didn't know Hatano was your stage name.

660
00:35:13,911 --> 00:35:16,314
Oh, sorry.

661
00:35:17,048 --> 00:35:19,750
But you can still call me Hatano. Ah…

662
00:35:20,751 --> 00:35:21,719
Sorry.

663
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:25,223
Um, so now, where are you…

664
00:35:26,524 --> 00:35:28,659
Spending the night in your car, I meant.

665
00:35:30,027 --> 00:35:31,662
At a roadside station.

666
00:35:34,966 --> 00:35:38,136
Hotaru told me everything.

667
00:35:38,202 --> 00:35:39,137
I see.

668
00:35:40,037 --> 00:35:44,408
I thought I’d play the role of her dad.

669
00:35:44,475 --> 00:35:46,477
Sure, I'll leave things to you.

670
00:35:46,544 --> 00:35:48,513
What, you're not going to stop me?

671
00:35:48,579 --> 00:35:49,514
Do you want me to?

672
00:35:50,047 --> 00:35:54,085
‪Well, I’m doing something
‪I probably shouldn’t, right?

673
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:55,586
Yeah, pretty much.

674
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:56,754
Right?

675
00:35:57,755 --> 00:36:00,391
- But you've already decided, right?
- Yes.

676
00:36:00,458 --> 00:36:02,627
- Good evening.
- Hello.

677
00:36:03,261 --> 00:36:05,363
This is her middle school
homeroom teacher, Mr. Sakuta.

678
00:36:05,429 --> 00:36:07,532
I'm the landlady, Inokashira.

679
00:36:07,598 --> 00:36:10,401
I'm Sakuta. Sorry for the sudden request.

680
00:36:10,468 --> 00:36:11,636
No worries.

681
00:36:11,702 --> 00:36:14,505
I'd appreciate it if you'd allow me
to park my car here for a while.

682
00:36:14,572 --> 00:36:16,440
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

683
00:36:18,910 --> 00:36:20,545
Sorry about this all of the sudden.

684
00:36:21,479 --> 00:36:22,313
Not at all.

685
00:36:22,813 --> 00:36:24,282
You don't have to sleep in your car.

686
00:36:24,782 --> 00:36:26,751
We have plenty of vacant rooms.

687
00:36:27,818 --> 00:36:28,719
- She's right.
- Oh, no.

688
00:36:28,786 --> 00:36:32,423
Living in the same building
as a student would be a little…

689
00:36:32,490 --> 00:36:36,727
Then, feel free to use the yard.

690
00:36:36,794 --> 00:36:37,762
Thank you.

691
00:36:37,828 --> 00:36:39,664
- Well then.
- See you.

692
00:36:42,633 --> 00:36:45,870
Sorry about this. Once I find a place,
I’ll move out immediately.

693
00:36:45,937 --> 00:36:47,004
No rush.

694
00:36:47,838 --> 00:36:49,607
Oh, and your lost item.

695
00:36:50,107 --> 00:36:51,842
I'm talking about your Santa sock.

696
00:36:53,110 --> 00:36:55,446
I tried searching for it,
but it was nowhere to be found.

697
00:36:55,513 --> 00:36:56,747
It's important to you, right?

698
00:36:57,315 --> 00:36:58,816
- I'll try looking for it again.
- Sorry.

699
00:36:59,317 --> 00:37:01,586
I already found it.

700
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:05,489
Oh, I see. That's great.

701
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:07,592
- I'll be heading back.
- Okay.

702
00:37:08,659 --> 00:37:09,493
See you.

703
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:16,934
See you.

704
00:37:22,106 --> 00:37:22,940
See you.

705
00:37:28,145 --> 00:37:29,313
May I come in?

706
00:37:37,355 --> 00:37:39,457
Why did you introduce him to this place?

707
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:43,027
He seemed troubled.

708
00:37:43,094 --> 00:37:45,896
If he finds out I live upstairs,
it’ll be bad.

709
00:37:46,397 --> 00:37:48,899
Oh, right.

710
00:37:48,966 --> 00:37:50,935
Don't give me that.

711
00:37:51,002 --> 00:37:52,203
I'm sorry.

712
00:37:53,537 --> 00:37:56,040
- Hey, do you want to eat?
- No.

713
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:01,746
Come to think about it, isn't it weird
that gays have kids to begin with?

714
00:38:02,980 --> 00:38:04,915
No, some people are married to women too.

715
00:38:07,084 --> 00:38:09,220
And the stage name part…

716
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:12,223
I pulled that off pretty slick, didn't I?

717
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:13,924
That was really forced.

718
00:38:14,525 --> 00:38:17,762
Also, how did you even know my dad's name…

719
00:38:19,030 --> 00:38:22,099
or the details of his divorce?

720
00:38:22,166 --> 00:38:25,269
I thought they’d ask,

721
00:38:25,336 --> 00:38:27,672
so I memorized everything in the notebook.

722
00:38:28,606 --> 00:38:31,542
So, does that mean you agree
to the contract?

723
00:38:31,609 --> 00:38:33,511
Just to be clear, I don’t need the money.

724
00:38:33,577 --> 00:38:35,513
- That's not negotiable.
- What?

725
00:38:35,579 --> 00:38:38,015
A contract needs to have consideration.

726
00:38:38,082 --> 00:38:40,318
I really don't need it.

727
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:43,688
You can just hold on to it for now.

728
00:38:44,221 --> 00:38:45,122
Huh?

729
00:38:45,690 --> 00:38:46,924
PARTY A, PARTY B

730
00:38:46,991 --> 00:38:48,893
Okay then, sign here.

731
00:38:58,669 --> 00:39:00,604
PARTY A: HOTARU KUSUNOKI
PARTY B: GENICHI HATANO

732
00:39:03,741 --> 00:39:04,575
What kind of house are you buying?

733
00:39:05,643 --> 00:39:06,644
Not buying.

734
00:39:08,245 --> 00:39:09,914
I can choose not to use it, right?

735
00:39:10,414 --> 00:39:11,449
Well, yeah.

736
00:39:12,650 --> 00:39:16,187
Okay now, I’ll whip up something simple.

737
00:39:21,492 --> 00:39:24,362
Right away, there's something
I need advice from you as my dad.

738
00:39:24,995 --> 00:39:25,896
What is it?

739
00:39:29,066 --> 00:39:30,101
CAREER SHEET

740
00:39:30,167 --> 00:39:31,635
I've got to submit this.

741
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:33,137
Haven't you filled it up already?

742
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:36,073
I'm not sure what to write.

743
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:39,043
- Any high school you'd like to go to?
- No.

744
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,847
Are there any jobs you'd like to do then?

745
00:39:42,913 --> 00:39:43,848
No.

746
00:39:47,318 --> 00:39:50,121
Why did you quit being a musician?

747
00:39:51,489 --> 00:39:52,323
Here.

748
00:39:53,023 --> 00:39:55,826
You were good enough to debut, right?

749
00:39:55,893 --> 00:39:59,397
It wasn’t because I was good at singing.
It was because I was gay.

750
00:40:01,499 --> 00:40:03,567
They wanted me to sing
in a tight tank top,

751
00:40:03,634 --> 00:40:06,203
speaking all campy, like I never do.

752
00:40:06,771 --> 00:40:09,039
They said it wouldn’t
be newsworthy enough otherwise.

753
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:11,008
If I hadn’t refused,

754
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:13,244
maybe I could’ve become
a professional musician.

755
00:40:17,214 --> 00:40:19,617
- Do you have any more <i>shishamo?</i>
- What, you want more?

756
00:40:20,284 --> 00:40:23,654
No, let’s send it to the person
who said that.

757
00:40:23,721 --> 00:40:26,090
And tell them that they don’t have
to poke holes in it.

758
00:40:26,157 --> 00:40:28,092
A <i>shishamo</i> bomb. Let's send it to them.

759
00:40:30,161 --> 00:40:32,496
Even I know that’s a mean thing to say.

760
00:40:35,132 --> 00:40:37,067
You don't have to do that for me.

761
00:40:38,669 --> 00:40:40,838
Have you come to hate singing?

762
00:40:44,642 --> 00:40:45,976
I’ve always loved it.

763
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:49,046
I thought about quitting.

764
00:40:50,214 --> 00:40:53,451
Every time I see my guitar,
it reminds me of that tight tank top,

765
00:40:53,517 --> 00:40:54,618
and it's annoying.

766
00:40:55,619 --> 00:40:59,190
But eventually, I realized that singing

767
00:41:00,524 --> 00:41:01,992
is something I still loved.

768
00:41:02,693 --> 00:41:04,595
That’s what love feels like, I guess.

769
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:06,630
What's that?

770
00:41:06,697 --> 00:41:09,633
I guess I’m just thinking
about it unconsciously…

771
00:41:10,167 --> 00:41:11,902
It feels like living the moment together.

772
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:16,707
I can’t go back
to who I was before meeting them.

773
00:41:17,708 --> 00:41:18,642
Something like that.

774
00:41:20,544 --> 00:41:22,012
What are we talking about?

775
00:41:23,347 --> 00:41:24,448
Who's them?

776
00:41:27,051 --> 00:41:28,052
Sorry, my bad.

777
00:41:29,086 --> 00:41:30,621
Do you have someone you like?

778
00:41:32,022 --> 00:41:32,857
No…

779
00:41:35,326 --> 00:41:36,360
Why do you ask?

780
00:41:36,994 --> 00:41:38,095
No reason.

781
00:41:38,963 --> 00:41:41,131
- Maybe <i>Santa Claus?</i>
- Yeah, right.

782
00:41:44,235 --> 00:41:45,836
Oh, no, no!

783
00:41:45,903 --> 00:41:47,171
Really?

784
00:41:47,238 --> 00:41:48,539
What's with that?

785
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:51,542
How nice of you to have
a lot of things you love.

786
00:41:53,244 --> 00:41:56,213
I don’t have any, and I don’t understand.

787
00:41:56,881 --> 00:41:57,715
You’ll find it.

788
00:41:59,116 --> 00:42:01,252
- Are you sure?
- Eventually. That's for sure.

789
00:42:01,919 --> 00:42:03,120
One or two things,

790
00:42:04,054 --> 00:42:05,022
definitely.

791
00:42:31,682 --> 00:42:32,716
I’VE LIKED YOU FOR A LONG TIME

792
00:42:32,783 --> 00:42:33,617
MEET ME AFTER SCHOOL ON MONDAY

793
00:42:33,684 --> 00:42:35,486
I forgot about this.

794
00:42:44,595 --> 00:42:46,063
Oh man.

795
00:42:47,364 --> 00:42:48,666
This is Saku's…

796
00:42:50,334 --> 00:42:52,336
<i>After the beep tone,</i>

797
00:42:52,403 --> 00:42:54,939
<i>please leave your name and message.</i>

798
00:42:55,973 --> 00:42:58,142
Hello, Mom? You've gotta hear this.

799
00:42:58,642 --> 00:43:01,712
My future self is always something

800
00:43:01,779 --> 00:43:03,347
I've never been able to imagine.

801
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,416
Like myself in high school.

802
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:07,351
Or working…

803
00:43:10,554 --> 00:43:12,289
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

804
00:43:13,657 --> 00:43:15,960
- What?
- I forgot to submit this yesterday.

805
00:43:16,694 --> 00:43:17,928
- Okay.
- <i>But</i>

806
00:43:17,995 --> 00:43:20,097
<i>my future self finding something</i>
<i>that I love</i>

807
00:43:20,164 --> 00:43:22,566
<i>is what I could slightly imagine.</i>

808
00:43:23,167 --> 00:43:24,635
<i>It sounds pretty fulfilling, huh?</i>

809
00:43:26,103 --> 00:43:28,505
<i>Did you ever have something</i>
<i>you loved, Mom?</i>

810
00:43:29,006 --> 00:43:30,541
<i>Something you wanted to do?</i>

811
00:43:31,141 --> 00:43:32,476
<i>Tell me when you return, yeah?</i>

812
00:43:33,177 --> 00:43:34,378
<i>Okay, bye.</i>

813
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:37,147
- This is my first time!
- That you reeled in a fish?

814
00:43:37,214 --> 00:43:38,248
No, fishing itself.

815
00:43:38,315 --> 00:43:40,517
You're missing out on life!

816
00:43:40,584 --> 00:43:41,652
This is really fun!

817
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:44,221
I think I might like it.

818
00:43:44,288 --> 00:43:45,356
Here goes!

819
00:43:46,724 --> 00:43:48,058
You dropped this.

820
00:43:48,959 --> 00:43:49,994
You dropped this!

821
00:43:52,796 --> 00:43:53,831
Thank you.

822
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:58,102
<i>Embezzlement of 30 million yen?</i>

823
00:43:58,736 --> 00:44:00,871
<i>A female employee is currently on the run.</i>

824
00:45:52,049 --> 00:45:54,017
Subtitle translation by: Jeffery
